{
  "_comment": [
    "K-pop group registry. This is the only curated file in the project.",
    "",
    "Why it exists: KOPIS genre CCCD ('popular music') mixes idol concerts with jazz",
    "salons, trot, indie club nights and acoustic sessions. Agency name alone is not",
    "enough — Antenna produces both PEPPERTONES (indie) and idol acts, and IST turned",
    "up on a wine-tasting gala. Matching a known group or member name is what actually",
    "separates them.",
    "",
    "Members are NOT listed here. They are derived from `prfcast` on the group's own",
    "performances, which SP05 found lists every member in full. Stage names are only",
    "recorded where we can state them without guessing — KOPIS gives legal names",
    "(SAKURA appears as 미야와키 사쿠라), and inventing a mapping would be a guess.",
    "",
    "`aliases` must be specific enough not to collide with ordinary words. Short or",
    "generic tokens are matched with word boundaries only — see matchGroup()."
  ],
